From ce7f9599c68873cb25d95f2b0fa1c503746c0ad9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:55:56 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] [python] Release the GIL in xbmc.getInfoLabel() and
 getInfoImage()

Both call CGUIInfoManager directly with the GIL still held. Many info
providers take the GUI lock on the way, for example anything that goes
through CGUIWindowManager::GetActiveWindowOrDialog() or GetWindow().

Since f939fe0460c the main thread can block on network I/O while it
holds that lock: CDirectoryFactory::Create() stats the item before
playback. When the item resolves to a URL served by a Python add-on
(a local media proxy, for example), the service cannot answer without
the GIL, the GIL holder waits for the GUI lock, and Kodi freezes until
curl gives up after 60 s. Any add-on polling an info label from a
background thread, as skin helpers do, is enough to trigger it.

Wrap both calls in a DelayedCallGuard, as executeJSONRPC() does, so the
GIL is released while the label is evaluated.

Assisted-By: Claude
(cherry picked from commit 9d1c26c23121f94887aa7c5b47d7a24a282bb2ae)
---
 xbmc/interfaces/legacy/ModuleXbmc.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/interfaces/legacy/ModuleXbmc.cpp b/xbmc/interfaces/legacy/ModuleXbmc.cpp
index 44bcde2..0ffb3b3 100644
--- a/xbmc/interfaces/legacy/ModuleXbmc.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/interfaces/legacy/ModuleXbmc.cpp
@@ -267,6 +267,7 @@ namespace XBMCAddon
     String getInfoLabel(const char* cLine)
     {
       XBMC_TRACE;
+      DelayedCallGuard dg;
       if (!cLine)
       {
         String ret;
@@ -286,6 +287,7 @@ namespace XBMCAddon
     String getInfoImage(const char * infotag)
     {
       XBMC_TRACE;
+      DelayedCallGuard dg;
       if (!infotag)
         {
           String ret;
-- 
